# The public flying-schedule repo must contain ONLY the calendar file the family
# subscribes to. Rather than listing what to exclude — which silently fails the
# moment a new kind of file appears — everything is ignored by default and the
# two intended files are whitelisted.
#
# This means a stray `git add -A` cannot publish anything new: roster
# screenshots, roster PDFs, email_trigger.log, roster.json, the pipeline
# scripts, .env or .roster_config. To add a genuinely new file to the public
# repo you must whitelist it here first, which is the point.
*
!.gitignore
!Kudzi-Flying-Schedule.ics

# Previously listed explicitly, kept here as a record of what must never be
# published: .roster_config, .env, *.pdf, *.py, roster.json, *.log,
# roster_screenshot.*, CLAUDE.md, PROGRESS.md, .claude/, .DS_Store
